  {"name": "Spec2.Basic",
   "moduleDocs":
   [{"scalars": [["title", "Spec-2 golden fixture"], ["type", "definition"]],
     "lists": [],
     "hasFrontmatter": true,
     "description":
     "The spec-2 facts of the inspector's report in one module: tagged definitions\nof every shape the validator has to tell apart (closed `Prop`, universe\npolymorphic, binders, `Type`-valued, a theorem, `private`), an untagged\nauxiliary, and theorems whose stored types walk — or fail to walk — as a chain\nof constants: every binder kind, duplicates, a self-edge, universe parameters,\na concrete level, a repeated level, a `max` level, a non-chain, an applied\nconstant, a definition of proof shape, a private theorem, a spec-1 frontmatter,\na declared axiom, and a `sorry`. The tag comes from the hook-less twin in\n`LaxCore.lean`, so the shapes the real hook refuses are here as facts."}],
   "imports": ["Init", "Init", "LaxCore"],
   "declCount": 30}],
